B.haQ=new A.qW(4,"Execution Work Packages (EWPs) / Construction (CWPs)","Translate WBS + EWPs into CWPs \u2014 executable field scopes. Each EWP/CWP should be tied to a specific area/system, executable by one crew or contractor, and have all prerequisites defined: approved IFC drawings, materials available, permits approved, access and site readiness.",B.NH,B.Jm,"For NDU Project, execution work packages are called CWPs when there is construction work for that scope; otherwise EWP, especially for Agile. They cascade from the WBS second level all the way to the lowest level possible \u2014 up to 8 levels if needed, until reaching the hours-of-work level. These work packages usually combine design and procurement or contract scope, especially at the 3rd to 5th levels.",B.dFc)
B.dDA=s(["WBS dictionary","Level 1 control accounts","Level 2 deliverable accounts"],t.s)
B.haR=new A.qW(1,"Deliverable-Based WBS","Build a Level 2\u20134 WBS structured around physical deliverables or systems \u2014 not departments. Typical top levels: Facility \u2192 Civil works \u2192 Structural \u2192 Mechanical systems \u2192 Electrical systems. This becomes the backbone for everything else.",B.mQ,B.Jm,"For NDU Project, the WBS goes to the second level (Level 2).",B.dDA)
B.c2z=new A.a1(983605,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.doi=s(["Engineering duration basis","Procurement lead-time register","Construction productivity rates"],t.s)
B.haS=new A.qW(6,"Estimate Durations Across All Domains","Estimate durations for engineering (design cycles, reviews), procurement (lead times, vendor timelines), and construction (crew productivity rates). Use consistent methods across all three to avoid mismatch.",B.c2z,B.acP,"For NDU Project, all three domains (Engineering, Procurement, Execution) must use a single, documented estimation method. See the Estimate Basis card below for the assumptions and data sources.",B.doi)
B.c2O=new A.a1(983984,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.dwO=s(["Gantt chart (EWPs + Procurement + CWPs)","Milestone register","Baseline start/finish dates"],t.s)
B.haT=new A.qW(10,"Develop the Time-Phased Schedule","Convert into a Gantt chart showing EWPs, procurement activities, and CWPs. Add milestones: design complete, contract awarded, equipment delivered, construction complete, commissioning start.",B.c2O,B.Jn,"For NDU Project, the Gantt tab (next to this Builder tab) renders the time-phased view and the milestone register.",B.dwO)
B.cxT=s(["Procurement Breakdown Structure (PBS)","Long-lead register","Vendor scope packages","RFQ/RFP plan"],t.s)
B.haU=new A.qW(3,"Procurement & Contracting Breakdown","From EWPs, identify all items that must be purchased or contracted. Break into long-lead equipment, bulk materials, and subcontracts. For each item, define procurement activities: scope definition \u2192 RFQ/RFP \u2192 bid evaluation \u2192 award \u2192 fabrication \u2192 delivery. Creates a Procurement Breakdown Structure (PBS) aligned to the WBS.",B.fI,B.Jm,"For NDU Project, any design that needs to feed into a procured item is identified in its package so that its scope is complete for sending to the vendor to build (mostly for waterfall but could apply to agile sometimes). Sits at the 3rd level of the WBS.",B.cxT)
B.djx=s(["Contract \u2192 CWP mapping","Vendor contract register","Subcontractor scope sheets"],t.s)
B.haV=new A.qW(8,"Align Contracts to Work Packages","Contracts should map cleanly to CWPs and procurement packages: each major CWP \u2192 contract or subcontract; each procurement package \u2192 vendor contract. Avoid contracts that cut across multiple CWPs (creates coordination chaos).",B.xu,B.Jn,"For NDU Project, the Contract Register should be filterable by CWP id so the team can trace every contract back to a single executable scope.",B.djx)
B.dgZ=s(["Baseline schedule (locked)","Engineering progress S-curve","Procurement expediting dashboard","Construction progress vs plan"],t.s)
B.haW=new A.qW(12,"Baseline and Control","Baseline the integrated schedule and track engineering progress vs release dates, procurement expediting vs delivery dates, and construction progress vs planned sequence.",B.fH,B.acQ,"For NDU Project, the baseline is locked from the Builder page. Variance reporting is then run from the Project Controls dashboards.",B.dgZ)
B.dE_=s(["CWP release gate checklist","Permit & access register","Predecessor completion log"],t.s)
B.haX=new A.qW(11,"Establish Schedule Readiness Rules","A CWP should not start unless all constraints are cleared: engineering complete, materials on site, permits approved, predecessors finished. This is the core of reliable execution planning.",B.NF,B.acQ,'For NDU Project, see the Schedule Readiness Rules card below \u2014 each gate must be cleared before a CWP moves from "Planned" to "In Progress".',B.dE_)
B.dhU=s(["Critical path diagram","Total project duration","Float report on non-critical paths"],t.s)
B.haY=new A.qW(7,"Build the Integrated Schedule Network (CPM)","Use the Critical Path Method (CPM) to calculate the full timeline. Key outputs: critical path across engineering, procurement, and construction; total project duration; float on non-critical paths. This step ensures procurement delays or design bottlenecks are visible early.",B.aog,B.Jn,'For NDU Project, CPM is run from the Schedule Builder via the "Run CPM" action above. Critical path drives staging decisions and forecast reporting.',B.dhU)
B.dkz=s(["Drawing register","Specification index","Calculation set","Bill of materials (BOM)","Code & standards matrix"],t.s)
B.haZ=new A.qW(2,"Engineering Work Packages (EWPs)","From each WBS element, define EWPs that produce the design outputs needed for execution: drawings, specifications, calculations, bill of materials, codes, requirements. EWPs must be complete enough to release for execution or construction (waterfall).",B.FA,B.Jm,"For NDU Project, these are the design packages that align with all requirements and applicable specifications. They sit at the 3rd level of the WBS to identify all design and engineering work needed for each scope element.",B.dkz)
